      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(gateway): add separate inline avatar size cap for agents.list projection",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`agents.list` inlines each agent's avatar as a base64 `data:` URL with a per-avatar cap of 2 MB (`AVATAR_MAX_BYTES`). Images carrying embedded metadata (C2PA provenance manifests, etc.) can easily hit that cap, ballooning the response.\n\n- **Observed**: 3 agents with PNG avatars → **4.15 MB `agents.list` response** (one avatar carried an embedded C2PA manifest).\n- **Projected**: 10 such agents → ~20 MB in a single RPC response.\n- **Impact**: Android client's default request timeout (15 s) was too short to receive a multi-MB `agents.list`, leaving the agent list empty on slow links. Mitigated client-side in #103248, but that's not a fix.\n\n## Linked Issue\n\n- Fixes #103265\n\n## Motivation\n\n`AVATAR_MAX_BYTES = 2 MB` was too generous for inline avatar data URLs. Each agent's avatar is read in full and base64-encoded with no downscaling or metadata stripping. A single ~2 MB PNG produces a ~2.7 MB base64 string.\n\n**Key design decision**: Rather than lowering the shared `AVATAR_MAX_BYTES` (which controls upload/acceptance), this PR introduces a separate `AVATAR_INLINE_MAX_BYTES = 256 KB` that only caps the inline projection in `resolveAgentAvatarUrlFromSource` (the function used exclusively by `agents.list` / `chat.startup` agent-list projection). The shared file opener and data-url reader retain the 2 MiB limit, so `assistant-avatar.ts` (dedicated avatar delivery via Control UI) is unaffected.\n\n## Changes\n\n5 files changed, +179/−3.\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `src/shared/avatar-limits.ts` | +6: added `AVATAR_INLINE_MAX_BYTES = 256 * 1024` |\n| `src/shared/avatar-policy.ts` | +6/−3: re-export `AVATAR_INLINE_MAX_BYTES` |\n| `src/agents/identity-avatar-file.ts` | +28/−3: inline cap in `resolveAgentAvatarUrlFromSource` with deduplicated warning |\n| `src/agents/identity-avatar-file.test.ts` | +59/−1: inline cap tests + production proof test |\n| `src/gateway/proof-avatar-cap.server.test.ts` | +83: real gateway WebSocket RPC proof test |\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Production path test (listAgentsForGateway)\n\n```\n3× 1.4 MB avatars payload: 1,456 bytes\n```\nFrom the original 4.15 MB (3 agents) to 1,456 bytes — **99.97% reduction**.\n\n### Real gateway RPC test\n\nWebSocket → `chat.startup` → `agentsList`, passes under both `gateway-server` and `gateway-methods` Vitest configs.\n\n### Full suite\n\n```bash\npnpm test src/agents/identity-avatar-file.test.ts   # 8/8 passed\npnpm test src/agents/identity-avatar.test.ts         # 14/14 passed\npnpm test src/gateway/proof-avatar-cap.server.test.ts # 2/2 passed\n```\n\n## Compatibility\n\n- **Upload/acceptance limit**: stays 2 MiB (`AVATAR_MAX_BYTES`)\n- **Inline projection cap**: 256 KiB (`AVATAR_INLINE_MAX_BYTES`) — only in agent-list RPC responses\n- **Dedicated avatar delivery** (Control UI / `assistant-avatar.ts`): unaffected, retains 2 MiB\n- Avatars between 256 KiB and 2 MiB remain accepted and stored but return `avatarUrl: undefined` in `agents.list`",
        "branch": "fix/avatar-cap-103265",
        "head_sha": "bd85f9eb575c33fe1fb848903b5ac59248316ca6",
